    <!-- §1 Overview -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="overview">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§1</div>
        <h2>System Overview</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        An operator at a central bank uses the Issuance tab to convert a cleared trade
        claim into a batch of cryptographically signed CVIB notes. Each note is minted
        from a denomination template, signed server-side with the issuing bank's Ed25519
        key, vault-encrypted (AES-256-GCM), packaged with a SHA-256 manifest, and
        distributed to the claiming commercial bank over email or SFTP. The workflow is
        gated by a supervisor clearance step and a 4-digit operator PIN before any note
        is minted.
      </p>

      <div class="dp-pane-grid">
        <div class="dp-pane dp-pane-left">
          <h3>Left Pane — Configuration</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Select cleared trade claim (source)</li>
            <li>Issuer identity (country, bank, governor)</li>
            <li>Asset code &amp; currency metadata</li>
            <li>Corridor identity &amp; funding lock</li>
            <li>Denomination &amp; note count</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-pane dp-pane-middle">
          <h3>Middle Pane — Execution</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Sovereign Clearance Status</li>
            <li>Execution pipeline (3 phases)</li>
            <li>Operator-PIN authorization gate</li>
            <li>Issuance registry activity feed</li>
            <li>Manifest verification</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-pane dp-pane-right">
          <h3>Right Pane — Properties</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Authorization snapshot</li>
            <li>Batch configuration</li>
            <li>Claiming institution</li>
            <li>Issuer public-key selection</li>
            <li>Packaging options (watermark, marking)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Key Concepts</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Concept</th><th>Definition</th><th>Example from UI</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Trade Claim</strong></td><td>A cleared cross-border obligation that authorises issuance. Selected from the <code>SELECT SOURCE</code> dropdown. No mint can begin without one.</td><td>— No active trade claims —</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Issuance Authorization</strong></td><td>Governance-cleared record linking the claim to a backing liquidity lock. Carries the authorization ID surfaced in Clearance Status.</td><td>INV-2026-167-002</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>CVIB Note</strong></td><td>A single Central Bank Issuance Bill — a true PNG bearer note with embedded metadata, QR, barcode, and Ed25519 signature.</td><td>₦200 denomination note</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>CVIB Batch</strong></td><td>A group of notes minted together under one authorization, sealed by a single SHA-256 manifest hash.</td><td>Batch ID (UUID)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Claiming Institution</strong></td><td>The commercial bank that receives the minted batch as bearer instruments.</td><td>WEMA BANK PLC · AACLZAJJ</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Clearing Source</strong></td><td>How an authorization reached a mintable state — either a <strong>supervisor-cleared trade claim</strong> (cross-border, l-CBDC) or an <strong>RTGS liquidity swap</strong> (domestic, pre-cleared d-CBDC). Surfaced in Sovereign Clearance Status. See §11.</td><td>RTGS Liquidity Swap (d-CBDC)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>RTGS Liquidity Swap</strong></td><td>A commercial bank's real-time gross settlement of fiat to the central bank, captured as an ISO 20022 <code>pacs.009</code> message and surfaced as a pre-cleared issuance source — the deposit itself backs the issuance.</td><td>RTGS-E2E-56a5123d…</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-info"><span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span><div>The header strip reports live node state — <strong>Node: AUTHORIZED</strong>, <strong>Connected: Mainnet</strong> — alongside overall system health, sync status, and global issuance counters. <strong>Sync with RTGS</strong> reconciles issuance totals against the real-time gross settlement ledger.</div></div>
    </div>

