    <!-- §3 Left Pane -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="left-pane">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§3</div>
        <h2>Left Pane — Issuance Configuration</h2>
      </div>

      <h3>Select Source</h3>
      <p>Editable QComboBox listing cleared issuance authorizations, populated from <code>GET /api/v2/issuance_authorizations</code>. The refresh button re-queries the registry. Until a source is selected the entire mint workflow is inert and the dropdown reads <code>— No active trade claims —</code>.</p>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-info"><span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span><div>SELECT SOURCE lists authorizations from <strong>both clearing sources</strong> — supervisor-cleared trade claims (l-CBDC, <code>L-{CCY}</code>) and RTGS liquidity swaps (d-CBDC, native <code>{CCY}</code>). Each entry shows its corridor, asset, amount and a <strong>🟢 READY TO MINT</strong> badge. See <a href="#rtgs">§11 — RTGS Settlement Clearing</a>.</div></div>

      <h4>On Selection — Configuration Cascade</h4>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Populate issuer identity</h4><p>Country, Central bank, Governor, City, Branch, Governance — read-only, derived from the authorising institution.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Populate asset / currency</h4><p>SWIFT/BIC, Symbol, Serial pattern, Currency no., IBAN, Country code, Coin symbol, ISO 4217, Coin name, Currency name.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Populate corridor identity</h4><p>Country, Central Bank, Currency, Governor, Total auth., FX rate, Liquidity, Funding lock — pulled from the backing corridor.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Enable denomination block</h4><p>Select count / denomination becomes active so the operator can size the batch.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3>Config Field Groups</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Fields</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Issuance config _draft</strong></td><td>Country, Central bank, Governor, City, Branch, Governance</td><td>Authorising institution (read-only)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Asset code _currency</strong></td><td>SWIFT/BIC, Symbol, Serial pattern, Currency no., IBAN, Country code, Coin symbol, ISO 4217, Coin name, Currency name</td><td>Currency registry</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Corridor identity</strong></td><td>Country, Central Bank, Currency, Governor, Total auth., FX rate, Liquidity, Funding lock</td><td>Corridor Ops backing lock</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Select count _denomination</strong></td><td>Note count, denomination template</td><td>Operator input</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §4 Middle Pane -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="middle-pane">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§4</div>
        <h2>Middle Pane — Execution</h2>
      </div>

      <h3>Sovereign Clearance Status</h3>
      <p>A live panel reflecting the governance gate that precedes minting. Bound to <code>GET /api/v2/issuance_authorizations/:auth_code</code>. Because SELECT SOURCE only lists claims with <code>state=cleared</code>, any claim the operator can select already resolves to a <em>Cleared</em> gate the moment the cascade loads — the panel reflects an approved authorization, not a pending one.</p>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example (selected claim)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Authorization ID</td><td>The cleared authorization reference</td><td>INV-2026-167-002</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Clearance Gate</td><td>Current governance state of the claim</td><td>Cleared</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Approved By</td><td>Supervisor who cleared the claim</td><td>[Supervisor ID]</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Clearing Source</td><td>Origin of the clearance decision</td><td>Governance tab · Four-Eyes</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-warn"><span class="dp-ci">⚠</span><div>Four-Eyes is enforced server-side. The dropdown can only surface cleared claims, so the standard path never sees a pending gate — but if an <em>uncleared</em> <code>auth_code</code> is submitted out-of-band (terminal/debug console), Package Authorization is rejected with HTTP&nbsp;409 <code>clearance_pending</code>. The client never makes the trust decision.</div></div>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-info"><span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span><div><strong>Two clearance postures.</strong> A <em>trade-claim</em> authorization shows <code>Clearance Gate: Passed</code>, <code>Approved By: Supervisor / …</code>, <code>Clearing Source: Regional Supervisor Desk</code>. An <em>RTGS</em> authorization (d-CBDC) instead shows <code>Clearance Gate: Cleared (Deterministic)</code>, <code>Approved By: RTGS System Core</code>, <code>Clearing Source: RTGS Liquidity Swap (d-CBDC)</code> — the fiat has already settled, so clearance is deterministic rather than discretionary. The client selects the posture from the authorization's <code>clearing_source</code> field. See <a href="#rtgs">§11</a>.</div></div>

      <h3>Issuance Execution Pipeline</h3>
      <p>Three sequential phases, surfaced as a tabbed strip. Each phase unlocks only when its predecessor reports success.</p>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Phase 1 — Package Authorization</h4><p>Operator enters the 4-digit PIN. POST /issuance_authorizations/:auth_code/cvib_batches → returns batch_id + per-note payloads.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Phase 2 — Vault Generation</h4><p>Per note: render denomination template, generate serial, embed zlib-compressed iTXt metadata, QR + Code-128 barcode, Ed25519 sign, AES-256-GCM vault-encrypt, write true PNG.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Phase 3 — Node Distribution</h4><p>ZIP notes + manifest.json, POST /cvib_batches/:batch_id/confirm_manifest, deliver to claiming bank via email or SFTP.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3>Operator PIN Gate</h3>
      <div class="dp-rule">PIN field accepts exactly 4 digits — the "Enter 4-Digit Operator PIN" button stays locked until 4 digits are present.</div>
      <div class="dp-rule">A cleared trade claim must be selected — empty source shows "Select a cleared trade claim from SELECT SOURCE above to begin."</div>
      <div class="dp-rule">PIN is validated server-side against the operator session; never stored client-side.</div>

      <h3>Issuance Registry — Activity Feed</h3>
      <p>Live feed of minting activity for the session. Empty state reads <strong>No Active Issuance Claims</strong> / "Select a trade authorization above to begin the minting workflow."</p>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Source</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>● Active counter</td><td>session mint state</td><td>Green dot when a batch is in flight</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Notes count</td><td>batch.note_count</td><td>"0 notes" until Phase 2 completes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Registry / Last Batch / Session Issued</td><td>session aggregates</td><td>Footer ledger summary</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §5 Right Pane -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="right-pane">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§5</div>
        <h2>Right Pane — Issuance Properties</h2>
      </div>

      <h3>Authorization Snapshot</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Issuance Authorization ID</td><td>The cleared authorization the batch mints against</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Asset Code</td><td>ISO 4217 currency of the batch</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Total Amount</td><td>Authorised face value</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Backing Lock ID</td><td>Corridor Ops liquidity lock collateralising issuance (dropdown)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Corridor</td><td>Bilateral corridor the batch flows through (dropdown)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Batch Configuration</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Issuance Authorization ID / Asset Code / Backing Lock ID / Corridor</td><td>Mirror of the snapshot, editable for batch override</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Allocated Serial Block</td><td>Serial range reserved for the batch</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Batch ID</td><td>UUID returned by Package Authorization</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Initial Holder / Holder ID</td><td>Claiming institution key IDs (may be empty at mint)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Issuer Key</td><td>Ed25519 signing key selector ("Select Issuer Key")</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Expiry Date</td><td>Optional batch expiry ("None" = non-expiring)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Authorization ID / Manifest Hash</td><td>Populated after seal in Phase 2/3</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Claiming Institution</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Example from UI</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Commercial Bank</td><td>WEMA BANK PLC</td></tr>
          <tr><td>City</td><td>City Name</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Branch</td><td>Branch Name</td></tr>
          <tr><td>BIC / SWIFT Code</td><td>AACLZAJJ</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Public Key Selection</h3>
      <p>Selects the issuer public key paired with the signing key. Example: <code>a03e7f5158ba2ffc9c683bce724da…</code>. The server verifies the chosen public key matches the IssuerKey referenced in Batch Configuration.</p>

      <h3>Packaging Options</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Values</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Watermark</td><td>Simulation Only | Production</td><td>Non-production modes scale notes to 70% and apply a diagonal SPECIMEN overlay — below the legal-tender threshold.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Marking</td><td>None (Original) | Specimen | Pilot | Sandbox</td><td>Controls header banding and CBDC technical-pilot markings.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-danger"><span class="dp-ci">⛔</span><div>Only <strong>Watermark = Production</strong> with <strong>Marking = None (Original)</strong> produces legal-tender notes at 100% scale. Every other combination is non-tender and watermarked SPECIMEN — never deliver a simulation batch to a commercial bank as live currency.</div></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §6 Lifecycle -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="lifecycle">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§6</div>
        <h2>Issuance Lifecycle</h2>
      </div>
      <p>The horizontal status pipeline at the top of the tab tracks the batch through five states: <strong>Draft → Preview → Authorization → Generation → Minted</strong>.</p>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Draft</h4><p>Trade claim selected, config + denomination set. Nothing committed. Right-pane properties editable.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Preview</h4><p>Operator reviews snapshot, claiming institution, and packaging options. Specimen preview rendered for non-production modes.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Authorization</h4><p>Operator PIN entered → Package Authorization returns batch_id + payloads. Requires cleared Sovereign Clearance Status.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Generation</h4><p>Notes minted, signed, vault-encrypted; manifest sealed with SHA-256.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Minted</h4><p>Batch confirmed and distributed to the claiming bank. Registry feed updated; notes enter the validation lifecycle.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §7 Buttons -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="buttons">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§7</div>
        <h2>Button-Level Behaviour</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Enter 4-Digit Operator PIN</span><span class="dp-btn-pane m">Middle Pane</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Inputs</div><div>Selected trade claim, 4-digit operator PIN</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /issuance_authorizations/:auth_code/cvib_batches {pin}</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Success</div><div>Returns batch_id + per-note payloads. Pipeline advances to Phase 2 — Vault Generation.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Failure</div><div>HTTP 409 if clearance pending; HTTP 401 on bad PIN. Branded alert dialog shown.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Sync with RTGS</span><span class="dp-btn-pane m">Header</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/rtgs/sync {node_id}</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Success</div><div>Global issuance + sync-status counters reconciled against the real-time gross settlement ledger.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Import metadata</span><span class="dp-btn-pane m">Registry Feed</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Inputs</div><div>Existing CVIB PNG/JPEG file</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Behaviour</div><div>Parses embedded metadata via magic-byte detection; PNG iTXt "Comment" chunk inflated (zlib) before parse.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Download / Verify Manifest</span><span class="dp-btn-pane m">Registry Feed</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>GET /cvib_batches/:batch_id/manifest</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Behaviour</div><div>Recomputes SHA-256 over the batch and compares to manifest_hash. Disabled until a batch is minted.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Refresh</span><span class="dp-btn-pane m">Registry Feed</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Behaviour</div><div>Re-queries the issuance registry for the active session and repaints the activity feed.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
