    <!-- §11 RTGS Settlement Clearing -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="rtgs">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§11</div>
        <h2>RTGS Settlement Clearing (d-CBDC)</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Issuance authorizations reach a mintable state through one of two clearing
        sources. Cross-border obligations clear through the <strong>supervisor / Four-Eyes
        governance gate</strong> as <em>linked</em> CBDC (l-CBDC). Domestic liquidity clears
        through the <strong>RTGS gateway</strong> as <em>domestic</em> CBDC (d-CBDC): when a
        commercial bank moves fiat to the central bank's settlement account over the
        real-time gross settlement network, that deposit is captured and surfaced as a
        pre-cleared issuance source — the settlement itself is the backing.
      </p>

      <h3>Clearing Source Comparison</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th></th><th>Trade Claim (l-CBDC)</th><th>RTGS Liquidity Swap (d-CBDC)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Origin</strong></td><td>Cross-border trade obligation</td><td>Domestic RTGS fiat settlement (ISO 20022 pacs.009)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Clearance</strong></td><td>Supervisor / Four-Eyes (discretionary)</td><td>Deterministic — pre-cleared out-of-band</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Asset type</strong></td><td><code>linked</code></td><td><code>domestic</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Asset code</strong></td><td><code>L-{CCY}</code> (e.g. L-ZAR)</td><td>native <code>{CCY}</code> (e.g. ZAR)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Backing</strong></td><td>Reserve lock on the source-side corridor</td><td>The settlement deposit self-funds</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Clearing Source label</strong></td><td>Regional Supervisor Desk</td><td>RTGS Liquidity Swap (d-CBDC)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Inbound RTGS Pipeline</h3>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>1 · Settlement received</h4><p>A commercial bank's RTGS network posts an ISO 20022 <code>pacs.009</code> message to <code>POST /api/v2/rtgs/inbound/pacs009</code> over mutual TLS with a shared-secret header. The raw payload is audited.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>2 · Idempotent ingest</h4><p>The message is parsed and keyed on <code>(BizMsgIdr, UETR)</code>. A duplicate returns <code>200 DUPLICATE_IGNORED</code>; a first-seen message advances.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>3 · Pre-cleared claim</h4><p>A trade claim is created and run through corridor verification. Domestic settlements self-fund; cross-border ones draw corridor headroom. On success the claim reaches <code>ready_to_mint</code> and broadcasts a sovereign clearance event.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>4 · Surfaced to operator</h4><p>The desktop client adopts the cleared claim into an IssuanceAuthorization (<code>auth_code: BC-RTGS-…</code>) so it appears in SELECT SOURCE with the d-CBDC clearance posture — ready to mint with no supervisor step.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-info"><span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span><div><strong>Domestic self-funding.</strong> An RTGS settlement is treated as its own backing — the fiat has already moved to the central bank, so a domestic d-CBDC swap clears deterministically to <code>ready_to_mint</code> without a separate corridor reserve. Cross-border RTGS still verifies corridor headroom and parks at <code>insufficient_corridor_liquidity</code> (awaiting Governor liquidity injection) if depleted.</div></div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-ok"><span class="dp-ci">✓</span><div><strong>Asset naming.</strong> Linked instruments are explicitly marked <code>L-{CCY}</code> because they are reserve-backed derivatives, not native currency. Domestic d-CBDC keeps the <strong>plain</strong> sovereign code (<code>ZAR</code>, not <code>D-ZAR</code>) — it is legal-tender currency, and the <code>asset_type: domestic</code> field carries the distinction.</div></div>

      <h3>Gateway Heartbeat</h3>
      <div class="dp-rule">The Corridor Ops gateway indicator polls <code>GET /api/v2/rtgs/status</code> and reports <strong>● RTGS Reserve: CONNECTED / IDLE / UNKNOWN</strong> with the time of the last settlement received.</div>
    </div>

